"A native procedure given a procedure that may wait, here on the standard
 input (C388): native code calls it and wants its answer at once, running
 it to its end where nothing may wait, so in kayak's async mode it could
 never be waited for. KFX refuses it; FX-26 takes it. A callback of an
 effect without `receive`, `await`, the standard input, a capture or an
 effect variable is taken, as `made-frames-x86_64.kfx`'s is."
(define-effect kfx (maxeff (read @globals) spin))
(define-type waiter (subr (conv fx) (maxeff (io stdin) spin) (int) int))
(define-type runner (subr (conv native) (maxeff (read @globals) spin) (int waiter) int))
(define* make (subr (maxeff (read @globals) (alloc @heap) (write @heap) (read @heap) spin (io native)) () runner)
  (lambda ()
    (let ((b (the (bloblet (fields) @heap) (make-bloblet 1))))
      (the runner (native-procedure (seal-code b))))))
(define main (subr kfx () string) (lambda () "x"))
